>> title: Corn Ribs, Air Fryer
>> category: Vegetables & Sides
>> tags: corn, air fryer, basket, side, snack, chile
>> counters: The Air Fryer & the Pot
>> aka: corn ribs, air fryer corn ribs, curled corn, elote ribs, quartered corn cobs
>> servings: 4
>> time: 30 min
>> slack: forgiving — a minute either side changes nothing; they tell you they are done by curling, and a flat rib is simply not there yet
>> washing-up: the basket, the bowl

>> step: Written for a preheated 5.7 L basket. From cold, add three minutes. A 3.5 L basket is two batches, not more minutes.
A cob only exists as a rib in a basket, which is why nothing here is a variant.

>> step: quarter the cobs lengthways, then toss in the bowl
Stand @corn on the cob{4}(husked, halved across) on end and cut each half down through the core into quarters, then toss in a #bowl{} with @olive oil{2%Tbs}, @smoked paprika{2%tsp}, @ground cumin{1%tsp}, @kosher salt{1 1/2%tsp}.

>> step: roast in the basket 200°C (400°F), 12–14 min, cut side up
Roast @&(~1)seasoned ribs{} in a preheated #air fryer basket{} at 200°C (400°F) for ~air fry{13%min}, one layer and cut side up.

>> step: at seven minutes a curled rib is nearly there, a flat one is not
Check @&(~1)ribs{} once.

>> step: toss hot in the same bowl
Toss @&(~1)corn ribs{} with @lime{1}(cut in wedges), @crumbled feta{2%oz}(55 g), @cilantro{2%Tbs}(chopped).
